{
    "schema_version": "1.2",
    "name": "youtube-analytics",
    "display_name": "YouTube Analytics",
    "public_catalog": {
        "visibility": "public",
        "category": "analytics_product",
        "onboarding_modes": [
            "connector_pull"
        ],
        "verification": {
            "status": "blocked",
            "reason_code": "live_evidence_not_ratified",
            "follow_up": "Ratify once a real YouTube channel connection exists (no test account 2026-07-21)."
        }
    },
    "auth_type": "google_direct",
    "module_kind": "kpi",
    "report_profiles": [
        {
            "id": "channel_daily",
            "display_name": "Channel performance (daily)",
            "metrics": [
                "views",
                "estimated_minutes_watched",
                "likes",
                "comments",
                "shares",
                "subscribers_gained",
                "subscribers_lost"
            ],
            "dimensions": [
                "date",
                "channel_id"
            ],
            "extraction_capabilities": {
                "row_limit": null,
                "filters_supported": true,
                "realtime": false
            },
            "extraction_path": "custom_pull",
            "_api_notes": "GET youtubeanalytics/v2/reports?ids=channel==MINE&dimensions=day&metrics=<additive core>. Synchronous. Full lifetime history at daily grain; re-pull a trailing window for late-settling data. channel_id stamped from channels.list(mine=true). Ratio metrics (averageViewDuration/Percentage) NOT extracted -- computed at the semantic layer (AD-4)."
        },
        {
            "id": "video_daily",
            "display_name": "Video performance (daily)",
            "metrics": [
                "views",
                "estimated_minutes_watched",
                "likes",
                "comments",
                "shares",
                "subscribers_gained",
                "subscribers_lost"
            ],
            "dimensions": [
                "date",
                "video",
                "channel_id"
            ],
            "extraction_capabilities": {
                "row_limit": null,
                "filters_supported": true,
                "realtime": false
            },
            "extraction_path": "custom_pull",
            "_api_notes": "reports.query with dimensions=day,video. Per-video daily grain."
        },
        {
            "id": "video_upload",
            "display_name": "Video uploads (events)",
            "metrics": [],
            "dimensions": ["date"],
            "events": ["video_upload"],
            "extraction_capabilities": {
                "row_limit": null,
                "filters_supported": false,
                "realtime": false
            },
            "extraction_path": "custom_pull",
            "landing": "context_events",
            "_api_notes": "Data API v3: channels.list(part=contentDetails,mine=true) -> uploads playlist id; playlistItems.list(part=snippet,playlistId=<uploads>,maxResults=50) paginated. snippet.publishedAt = event_date (YYYY-MM-DD); snippet.title = label. Scope youtube.readonly already present -- no new scope. 1 quota unit per page (vs 100 for search.list)."
        }
    ],
    "canonical_event_mapping": {
        "video_upload": "video_upload"
    },
    "canonical_metric_mapping": {
        "views": "views",
        "estimatedMinutesWatched": "estimated_minutes_watched",
        "likes": "likes",
        "comments": "comments",
        "shares": "shares",
        "subscribersGained": "subscribers_gained",
        "subscribersLost": "subscribers_lost"
    },
    "canonical_dimension_mapping": {
        "day": "date"
    },
    "error_map": {
        "400": "invalid_request",
        "401": "auth_expired",
        "403": "permission_denied",
        "404": "permission_denied",
        "429": "provider_transient",
        "500": "provider_transient"
    },
    "_error_map_note": "VERIFIE le 2026-07-21. YouTube APIs return the standard Google error envelope { error: { code, message, errors[]:{reason, domain} } }. No stable numeric subcodes actionable beyond HTTP status, so the map is keyed on status: 401->auth_expired, 403->permission_denied (also covers insufficientPermissions -- e.g. a monetary metric requested without the yt-analytics-monetary scope), 404->permission_denied, 400->invalid_request (bad metric+dimension combo, e.g. liveOrOnDemand+averageViewPercentage), 5xx->provider_transient. IMPORTANT shim (mirrors gsc/google): Google returns quota-exceeded as a 403 with reason quotaExceeded/dailyLimitExceeded -- the connector routes such a 403 to core.quota.RateLimitError (breaker), NOT permission_denied. A 429 (userRateLimitExceeded/rateLimitExceeded) also raises RateLimitError.",
    "account_topology": {
        "_comment": "The reporting entity is a single YouTube CHANNEL. Standard flow: ids=channel==MINE targets the connected user's channel; discover_accounts resolves it via Data API channels.list(mine=true) -> {id, title}. One token -> one channel (non-MCN). Content-owner (MCN) mode (ids=contentOwner==<name>, onBehalfOfContentOwner) reports across many channels with the 'channel' dimension -- a later extension. Access-check = a 1-row reports.query on the selected channel. No *_CHANNEL_ID env var (doctrine).",
        "levels": [
            {
                "id": "channel",
                "label": "Channel"
            }
        ],
        "selection_level": "channel",
        "discovery": {
            "callable": "discover_accounts"
        }
    },
    "quota": {
        "window_seconds": 100,
        "budget_points": 720,
        "read_cost": 1,
        "write_cost": 1,
        "_rate_limit_note": "VERIFIE le 2026-07-21. TWO separate quota pools: (1) Data API v3 = 10,000 units/day (channels.list=1 unit; avoid search.list=100) -- discovery only, negligible. (2) Analytics API v2 (reports.query) = a SEPARATE pool (not the 10k), high daily ceiling, binding constraint = a per-100s per-user rate cap. Budget 720 points / 100s is a conservative pacing floor; the true ceiling is read live from the Cloud Console Quotas panel. 429 rateLimitExceeded (and 403 quotaExceeded) -> RateLimitError (breaker + backoff)."
    },
    "widget_ref": "ui://core/daily-report",
    "source_capabilities": {
        "contract_version": "1",
        "field_discovery": {
            "mode": "static",
            "allowed_targets": []
        },
        "fields": [
            {
                "field_id": "views",
                "source_field": "views",
                "kind": "metric",
                "physical_type": "integer",
                "description": "Number of times a video was viewed. Additive.",
                "semantic_hints": ["engagement", "count"],
                "canonical_target": "views",
                "aggregation": "sum",
                "non_additive": false
            },
            {
                "field_id": "estimated_minutes_watched",
                "source_field": "estimatedMinutesWatched",
                "kind": "metric",
                "physical_type": "integer",
                "description": "Total minutes users watched. Additive. (averageViewDuration = this*60/views is computed at the semantic layer, never stored.)",
                "semantic_hints": ["engagement", "count"],
                "canonical_target": "estimated_minutes_watched",
                "aggregation": "sum",
                "non_additive": false
            },
            {
                "field_id": "likes",
                "source_field": "likes",
                "kind": "metric",
                "physical_type": "integer",
                "description": "Positive ratings (likes). Additive.",
                "semantic_hints": ["engagement", "count"],
                "canonical_target": "likes",
                "aggregation": "sum",
                "non_additive": false
            },
            {
                "field_id": "comments",
                "source_field": "comments",
                "kind": "metric",
                "physical_type": "integer",
                "description": "Number of comments users left. Additive.",
                "semantic_hints": ["engagement", "count"],
                "canonical_target": "comments",
                "aggregation": "sum",
                "non_additive": false
            },
            {
                "field_id": "shares",
                "source_field": "shares",
                "kind": "metric",
                "physical_type": "integer",
                "description": "Times shared via the Share button. Additive.",
                "semantic_hints": ["engagement", "count"],
                "canonical_target": "shares",
                "aggregation": "sum",
                "non_additive": false
            },
            {
                "field_id": "subscribers_gained",
                "source_field": "subscribersGained",
                "kind": "metric",
                "physical_type": "integer",
                "description": "Times users subscribed. Additive.",
                "semantic_hints": ["audience", "count"],
                "canonical_target": "subscribers_gained",
                "aggregation": "sum",
                "non_additive": false
            },
            {
                "field_id": "subscribers_lost",
                "source_field": "subscribersLost",
                "kind": "metric",
                "physical_type": "integer",
                "description": "Times users unsubscribed. Additive.",
                "semantic_hints": ["audience", "count"],
                "canonical_target": "subscribers_lost",
                "aggregation": "sum",
                "non_additive": false
            },
            {
                "field_id": "date",
                "source_field": "day",
                "kind": "dimension",
                "physical_type": "date",
                "description": "Reporting day (YYYY-MM-DD) from the 'day' dimension. Full lifetime history at daily grain.",
                "semantic_hints": ["date"],
                "canonical_target": "date",
                "aggregation": "none",
                "non_additive": false
            },
            {
                "field_id": "video",
                "source_field": "video",
                "kind": "dimension",
                "physical_type": "string",
                "description": "Video resource id (group-by + filter).",
                "semantic_hints": ["content", "identifier"],
                "canonical_target": "video",
                "aggregation": "none",
                "non_additive": false
            },
            {
                "field_id": "channel_id",
                "source_field": "channel_id",
                "kind": "dimension",
                "physical_type": "string",
                "description": "The reporting entity: YouTube channel id. Stamped on every row (from channels.list(mine=true)).",
                "semantic_hints": ["identifier"],
                "canonical_target": "channel_id",
                "aggregation": "none",
                "non_additive": false
            },
            {
                "field_id": "video_upload",
                "source_field": "snippet.publishedAt",
                "kind": "event",
                "physical_type": "datetime",
                "description": "Date a video was published on the channel (snippet.publishedAt from Data API v3 uploads playlist). label_source_field = snippet.title. Persisted as a context_events pulse (value null, event_type video_upload).",
                "semantic_hints": ["event"],
                "label_source_field": "snippet.title",
                "canonical_target": "video_upload",
                "aggregation": "none",
                "non_additive": false
            }
        ],
        "reports": [
            {
